tanh}⁡{x}^{5},$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $5{x}^{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534976 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0bc32c07-1675-5c17-a61b-a851fe6dbaf3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186534976 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{({x}^{5})}^{2}}\\cdot {({x}^{5})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{10}}\\cdot 5{x}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{1-{x}^{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535003 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535003 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342666" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535003 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535003 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nCalculate ${g}^{′}(x)$ for $g(x)={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3).$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)\\,+$ | $4{e}^{x}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535003 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40534571-9b68-5a71-b2eb-96fad07c5254" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535003 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAnd the product rule is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}(u\\cdot v)}{\\text{d}x}={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, chain rule, and  formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{x})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3))}^{′} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(4x+3)}^{′} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+\\frac{4{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535026 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535026 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341959" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535026 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535026 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=4\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(3x-4),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535026 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "727d2976-e027-5f8e-a059-0575427eb806" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535026 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(4\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(3x-4)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(3x-4)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3x-4)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (3x-4)^{′} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3x-4)^{2}-1}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{(3x-4)^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535042 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535042 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342458" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535042 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535042 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=-\\sqrt{7}\\,\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535042 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "973108cd-4a12-5f7e-8def-c33e7591ffaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535042 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-3{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{3{x}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535089 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535089 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96426" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535089 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535089 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x-1),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535089 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd040bd9-e3ef-5708-a352-cc4c61514e23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535089 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x-1)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (2x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4{x}^{2}-4x+1)-1}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-4x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4x(x-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(x-1)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535099 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186535106 #edb/ref 1759218